values ($cw$merge-intervals$cw$, $cw$Merge the Intervals$cw$, $cw$You are given closed intervals on a number line. Intervals that overlap or touch (share an endpoint) merge into one.

### Input
The first line contains an integer `n`. Each of the next `n` lines contains two integers `l` and `r`.

### Output
Print two integers separated by a space: the number of intervals after merging, and their total length (the sum of `r - l` over the merged intervals).

### Constraints
- 1 ≤ n ≤ 100000
- -10^9 ≤ l ≤ r ≤ 10^9$cw$, $cw$medium$cw$, $cw$[{"input":"4\n1 3\n2 6\n8 10\n10 12","output":"2 9","explanation":"Merged: [1,6] and [8,12]. Lengths 5 + 4 = 9."},{"input":"1\n5 5","output":"1 0"}]$cw$::jsonb)
on conflict (slug) do update set
  title = excluded.title, statement_md = excluded.statement_md,
  difficulty = excluded.difficulty, samples = excluded.samples;
